WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:01.640
Tarik Cohen's comin' to New York
to eat

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:03.520
at a Jewish deli
with Simms and Lefkoe?

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:04.680
Oy vey!

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.880
♪♪

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.280
When I heard there was a guy
in the NFL, Simms

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:16.120
named Tarik Cohen,
I said, "Mwah.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:17.800
L'chaim. We've got ourselves

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:20.600
finally, a Jewish running back,"
and then I found out

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:23.920
not only have you never been
to a bar mitzvah

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:27.000
not only have you never had
Jewish food, you're not Jewish.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.840
- Sadly, no.
- Sadly, no.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:30.320
I appreciate the "sadly."
- Yeah.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:32.000
- "Cohen" though.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.440
I mean, that's in the
Mount Rushmore of Jewish names.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.760
- It really is.
- I am 100 percent Jewish.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.600
- Yeah.
- What I want to give to you

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:42.720
is the full Jewish experience.
I can call it a Jewish combine

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:45.720
to making you feel
like a true Jewish man.

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:47.480
Are you ready to take
this journey with me?

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.240
- Oh, yeah, I'm definitely ready.
- OK.

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:51.480
- L'chaim.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:52.800
- L'chaim!
- L'chaim.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:55.440
♪♪

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:58.480
[Bell dinging]

00:00:58.480 --> 00:00:59.880
- This is our first dish.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:02.880
This is a customary
Jewish breakfast.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:04.240
Do you want to take a guess
as to what

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:05.720
is in front of you right now?

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:07.640
- Sushi.
- Sushi.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:10.760
It is not sushi.
It is smoked salmon.

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:12.000
What do you think of it?

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.840
- Cream cheese and fish?
- Exactly.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.520
- Man.
- Yes, "man" is right.

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:17.000
- All right, so
don't be afraid of it.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:20.040
- No, I'm not.
- So why don't you pick it up?

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:21.520
- Oh, that was a——oh, my gosh.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:22.800
- Hold on.

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:27.560
- I don't like it.

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:29.480
- You don't?
Do you mind if I have a bite?

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:30.840
- Damn.
- You can have all the bites.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:34.520
- Ugh.
- I mean, it's perfect.

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:39.720
This is a Jewish deli staple,
and it's not just what it is—

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:42.200
- [Laughing] His eyes.
- It's the size of it, OK?

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:45.440
- Yeah.
- This is a pastrami on rye.

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:48.400
And do you see
how much meat is on that?

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:50.120
- Yeah.
- That's not just special.

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:51.680
- It's a little excessive.
- Can't miss it.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:52.720
- He looked at that like it was

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:53.800
a blitzing linebacker
when it came in.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:56.560
He, like, literally looked at it
and was like—

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:57.920
- Why don't you bite into that?
- All right.

00:01:57.920 --> 00:01:59.720
Let's see, which one—hmm.

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:00.800
- And this is part of the process,
too

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:02.520
the strategy of how
to bite the sandwich.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:04.120
- I can see that.

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:06.760
- I'm gonna go ahead
and try to flatten him.

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:08.480
- Nice.
I think he's gonna like this.

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:09.320
- You think he'll like it?

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:11.120
- I feel pretty
confident about it.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:12.440
- I really give him credit
for havin' the guts

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:14.160
to just dive in there, though.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:16.000
- Why is there no cheese
or nothin' on it though?

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.800
Cheese, mayonnaise
or somethin'?

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:21.120
- Well, that wouldn't be kosher.
We have one more.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:24.640
This is the Cadillac
of Jewish food.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:27.760
Tarik Cohen,
I'd like to introduce you

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:33.200
to your new favorite food,
matzo ball soup.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:35.640
- Matzo ball.
- Matzo ball.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:37.320
Have you heard
of matzo balls before?

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:39.520
- Mozzarella?
- Mozzarella

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:41.680
not the same thing.
This is not cheese.

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:43.600
- There's no cheese in there?
- There's no cheese.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.120
You thought matzo balls
had cheese, too?

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:47.200
- I totally did.
- So the best way to do this

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.600
is to take your spoon

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.240
take a little piece
of the matzo ball

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:52.000
get a little bit
of soup in there.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.400
- Oh, it's soft.
- It's very soft.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.360
♪♪

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:57.600
And there it is.

00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:59.040
- That's good.
- That's the 10 out of 10.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:00.240
- It's like chicken noodle soup,
really.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:01.480
- It's chicken noodle soup.

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:05.120
♪♪

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:09.640
The second part of our
Jewish combine is Jewish slang.

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:11.160
- OK.
- Not only do I want you to eat

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:13.880
like a Jew,
I want you to talk like a Jew.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:16.040
So here's the first word.
- This is gonna be fun.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:17.880
- It is.
- Schmooth.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:19.600
- Schmooze.

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:20.920
What do you
think schmooze means?

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:22.440
- Good sleep.
- Good sleep?

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:23.880
Oh, like a—

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:25.520
- Man, I'mma go schmooze.
- I'mma go schmooze.

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:27.680
- I'm about to schmooze.
- So, a schmooze is actually

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:29.760
to, like, kinda
talk somebody up.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:31.360
- "Hey, I like your play calls,
Matt Nagy."
- Yeah.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:33.240
- "That's a really creative one."
- "Throw me the ball."

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:34.800
- You're schmoozing him so he
gives you the ball.
- You're schmoozing, yeah.

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:36.120
- You schmooze, you win.
- Right.

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:38.160
- Next word. Ooh!

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:41.360
Good luck sayin' this one.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:43.800
- Chootz-pah.
- Hootz-pah.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:45.160
- Ah, chutzpah.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:48.280
- You gotta get a "heh."
- Chutzpah!

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:50.360
- Oh!
- "We were in the team meeting

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:52.000
and Tarik Cohen stood up
and said

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.520
'I don't like that play.'

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:56.000
Tarik's got a lot of chutzpah."

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.280
- Like, balls.
- Yeah.

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:04.440
- Exactly. This is the Jewish
slang phrase of all generations.

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:06.160
- Oy vey.
- Oy vey.

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:07.600
What do you think it is?

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:10.040
- "Tarik Cohen was supposed to run
the slant route

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:11.760
and he ran the go route.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:13.360
Oy vey, Tarik Cohen."

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:16.160
- Or it's like,
"All those pickles for me?

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:17.400
Oy vey."
- Oh, yeah, I got you.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:19.040
So it's good and bad.

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:20.560
- It can be everything.
- OK, good.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:21.800
That's the one
I'mma use right there.

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:23.600
- You have aced
the Jewish combine.

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:25.120
And I have a gift for you.

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:26.840
- Oy vey.
- Oy vey.

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:29.640
I give you
a Chicago Bears yarmulke.

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:33.760
- It's a Jewish fitted cap.
- A Jewish fitted cap, yes.

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:35.720
Oh, my gosh,
it looks so beautiful.

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:37.400
- Perfect.
- Simms, you're not out of here.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:39.040
- Oooh.
- A Giants yarmulke.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:41.400
- I like it.
- Put that bad boy on.

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:45.280
- Yeah!
- And I have an Eagles yarmulke.
Now we celebrate.

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:47.440
Let's give it up for him.

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:54.120
- Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:56.000
- Hey!
- L'chaim!

